      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "2.2 SLM process and heat treatment",
          "quote": "The deposited alloy was prepared by BLT-A300 equipment from Xi'an Bright Laser Technologies Co., Ltd., the composition of which was determined by ICP-AES (shown in Table 1). Argon was used as the shielding gas, and the preheating temperature of the substrate was 80 °C. Printing begins when the oxygen content in the cabin is below 200 ppm.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e660e3e6a79ffe2a:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 4,
          "section": "3.1 Parameters optimization of SLM process",
          "quote": "Comparing the mechanical properties of the alloys with different parameters, sample formed at 350 W/1300 mm/s has better mechanical properties. The horizontal yield strength (YS), ultimate tensile strength (UTS) and elongation (EL) of the alloy are 353 MPa, 589 MPa and 3.8%, while the vertical YS, UTS and EL are 332 MPa, 529 MPa and 2.0%, respectively. As is mentioned above, the forming quality of the alloy under this process is also preferable, so it was selected as the optimal process parameter, with which the subsequent heat treatments were explored.",
          "table": "Table 3",
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e660e3e6a79ffe2a:part:001"
        }
